{"name":"White Smoke","hex":"#f5f5f5","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"white smoke","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["White-colored smoke serving as an announcement to the outside world that a conclave has chosen a new Pope.","An event of reaching an agreement."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/white_smoke"}],"entries":[{"title":"X11 color names","blocks":[{"text":"In computing, on the X Window System, X11 color names are represented in a simple text file, which maps certain strings to RGB color values. It was traditionally shipped with every X11 installation, hence the name, and is usually located in <X11root>/lib/X11/rgb.txt. The web colors list is descended from it but differs for certain color names."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/X11_color_names"},{"title":"Conclave","blocks":[{"text":"A conclave is a gathering of the College of Cardinals convened to appoint the pope of the Catholic Church. Catholics consider the pope to be the apostolic successor of Saint Peter and the earthly head of the Catholic Church."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1c/Cappella_Sistina_-_2005.jpg/330px-Cappella_Sistina_-_2005.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Conclave"},{"title":"Smoke","blocks":[{"text":"Smoke is an aerosol emitted when a material undergoes combustion or pyrolysis, together with the quantity of air that is entrained or otherwise mixed into the mass. It is commonly an unwanted by-product of fires, but may also be used for pest control (fumigation), communication, defensive and offensive capabilities in the military, cooking, or smoking. It is used in rituals where incense, sage, or resin is burned to produce a smell for spiritual or magical purposes. It can also be a flavoring agent and preservative."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f3/Ognisko_ubt_0126.jpeg/330px-Ognisko_ubt_0126.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Smoke"},{"title":"White","blocks":[{"text":"White is the lightest color and is achromatic. It is the color of objects such as snow, chalk, and milk, and is the opposite of black. White objects fully reflect and scatter all the visible wavelengths of light. White on television and computer screens is created by a mixture of red, blue, and green light. The color white can be given with white pigments, especially titanium dioxide."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e2/Delphinapterus_leucas_2.jpg/330px-Delphinapterus_leucas_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/White"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5d/Shades_of_red.png/500px-Shades_of_red.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5d/Shades_of_red.png/500px-Shades_of_red.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AShades_of_red.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/11/Domus_Sanctae_Marthae_from_the_Dome_of_St._Peter%27s.jpg/500px-Domus_Sanctae_Marthae_from_the_Dome_of_St._Peter%27s.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/11/Domus_Sanctae_Marthae_from_the_Dome_of_St._Peter%27s.jpg/1280px-Domus_Sanctae_Marthae_from_the_Dome_of_St._Peter%27s.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/11/Domus_Sanctae_Marthae_from_the_Dome_of_St._Peter%27s.jpg/500px-Domus_Sanctae_Marthae_from_the_Dome_of_St._Peter%27s.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Since the 2005 papal conclave, the cardinal electors reside in the Domus Sanctae Marthae for the length of the conclave.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ADomus_Sanctae_Marthae_from_the_Dome_of_St._Peter's.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d4/Cardinal_Camerlengo_certifying_a_papal_death.JPG/330px-Cardinal_Camerlengo_certifying_a_papal_death.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d4/Cardinal_Camerlengo_certifying_a_papal_death.JPG/330px-Cardinal_Camerlengo_certifying_a_papal_death.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The camerlengo proclaiming a papal death","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACardinal_Camerlengo_certifying_a_papal_death.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f2/John_Paul_II_funeral_long_shot.jpg/500px-John_Paul_II_funeral_long_shot.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f2/John_Paul_II_funeral_long_shot.jpg/500px-John_Paul_II_funeral_long_shot.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Cardinals, bishops and priests attending the funeral of Pope John Paul II","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AJohn_Paul_II_funeral_long_shot.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/48/Folded_conclave_ballot.jpg/330px-Folded_conclave_ballot.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/48/Folded_conclave_ballot.jpg/330px-Folded_conclave_ballot.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Cardinals formerly used these intricate ballot papers, one of which is shown folded above. The text Latin reads \"Name\" and \"Signature\" at bottom, with the middle text translating to, \"I choose as Supreme Pontiff my most reverend lord, the Lord Cardinal [name].\" Currently, the ballots are simple cards, folded once, like a note card, with the words \"I elect as Supreme Pontiff\" printed in Latin on them.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AFolded_conclave_ballot.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d9/Card._Mahony%27s_Scrutiny_Ballot%2C_2013.jpg/500px-Card._Mahony%27s_Scrutiny_Ballot%2C_2013.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d9/Card._Mahony%27s_Scrutiny_Ballot%2C_2013.jpg/1280px-Card._Mahony%27s_Scrutiny_Ballot%2C_2013.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d9/Card._Mahony%27s_Scrutiny_Ballot%2C_2013.jpg/500px-Card._Mahony%27s_Scrutiny_Ballot%2C_2013.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Today, cardinal electors receive copies of multiple ballot cards, scrutiny ballots, and a copy of Ordo Rituum Conclavis (Order of Conclave Rites). Shown above are the ballot papers of Cardinal Roger Mahony used in the 2013 conclave.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACard._Mahony's_Scrutiny_Ballot%2C_2013.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b0/Conclave_1903_scrutin.jpg/500px-Conclave_1903_scrutin.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b0/Conclave_1903_scrutin.jpg/500px-Conclave_1903_scrutin.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Scrutiny during the conclave of 1903","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AConclave_1903_scrutin.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a9/Konklave_%E2%80%93_p%C3%A1len%C3%AD_